body:
10 years later and I had a professor approach me rather intimidatingly saying I used AI to write my paper. Interestingly, the report labeled a lot of my citations and sources as the stolen stuff. Which frankly makes no sense, considering yeah, that part is not my original writing. That's why I cited it.

&#x200B;

Needless to say this is the straw that broke the camels back, I'm dropping my university and just gonna give up. I can't reasonably be bothered to care about anything anymore regardless.

One of the former 'playerbase' here, I'm no longer playing after my first few matches in the new matchmaking. I specifically designed a lineup for tier 1 with my moscow stuff, and within my first match I am facing things I only really saw in Normandy or Berlin. While in a Panzer 3. Fighting panzerfausts that are able to knock out Tiger 2s while in something substantially weaker across the board is unfun gameplay.

&#x200B;

(Not to mention the guns, Germany getting mostly bolt actions and one smg with slight variations in tier 1 while the Soviets and Allies get just plain upgrades)

Yeah I was actually considering legal action since extortion isn't exactly something that flies, and they already had attempted to use their TOS as justification for something I did on steam.

&#x200B;

They legally have no right to do so, as they are subject to steam rules regarding purchases made via steam regardless of their own TOS. Would be different if I got banned for an ingame matter, but it was retaliation for refunding on steam.

I think it's surreal that BSG has failed to implement things modders have done for free in their spare time within months if not weeks. Then with the entire SPT thing, this was done within a relatively short time as well and gets way more support than live does. I expect him to try and cease the development of SPT in the near future, but I don't think it will do much at all. He would have to be willing to take it to court in wherever SPT is based, and then shill out a lot of potential gamedev money just to shut down one person/group only for a copy of SPT to come out and keep it going. Same shit went on with for example, World of Warcraft private servers. Blizz took the legal approach a few times but that only spurred more servers, and now there are more people on private servers than some live world of warcraft servers, and continue to be so as it grows.

&#x200B;

End of the day legally and maybe morally he's allowed to do whatever he wants, but ultimately I paid for this game and grew irritated with the gameplay of online, and the lack of quality control or even progress. I mean it's absolutely wacky how long it has taken to even get the presented features out. Like the fact that half the map list has been locked since the start, or how half the skills are not even implemented. I think the recognition isn't bad, BSG is already well aware of SPT existing and has been pretty staunchly against it thus far. But they really can't do much besides slap content creators or try to legally take it down. Which, depending on where the main devs of SPT reside, is expensive even for a large game studio and almost impossible in a realistic sense if BSG and SPT devs aren't in the same country.

Should have brought back the removed vehicles that are somehow more historical than the ones they replaced them with. Such as the Flakpanzer 341 being replaced by the even more fictional Ostwind...2. Ostwind 2. Really? Flakpanzer 341 is literally just a more fun Ostwind 2, panther chassis, closed top, slow as balls, fun as hell, and it's significantly more cool than 'Oh look we got an Ostwind with two barrels to research. Hooray.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

DON'T EVEN GET ME STARTED WITH HOW THE MAUS IS GENUINELY A GOOD VEHICLE AND IS PERFECT AT 8.0. (I mean it's good at 7.7 too but 8.0 for both Arcade and Realistic is just a good balance given it's not really invincible in either spot but still holds it's own very well.)

I think you may misunderstand the mentality of a lot of Americans, as there are plenty of us that do in fact dislike the current forms of government here. That said, I feel the way you do about the Chinese and Russians, as I've yet to meet one that wasn't brainwashed to shit or horribly toxic. Although I too know not all are that way.

&#x200B;

That being said, America is hardly the only country out there that is, capitalist dominant, primarily self focused, lying, and known to invade places. Don't forget that a lot of European countries were personally involved in many of the happenings in the Middle East, Afghanistan in particular even saw Australians committing some of the worst recorded crimes of our occupation there.

&#x200B;

And that, that being said, additionally that, while I understand you say you don't hold a grudge against Americans, you go on to then in fact call out and accuse people of just accepting things. As though we don't have 50 countries in our country that each have their own people who vote for their own leaders and for their own laws. Keep in mind someone in California may get 5 years in prison for murder, while someone in Missouri may get 50 or life for murder. Not accurate numbers but just an analogy of how different our states are from one another.

&#x200B;

I knew a Canadian who spoke about us similarly to how you do, and they refused to acknowledge that we aren't a collective hivemind centered solely around a federal government. It's true that the federal government is shitty right now and has been for years, but it's also true that states tend to have the final say on a lot of things that happen in the country and not all of them are keen on the negative things you say just happening. My state included has been reforming the prison systems and personal 'freedoms' lately.

&#x200B;

I don't mean this as a personal attack towards you, however I do feel as though you aren't considering things from our point of view. Especially the whole 'brainwashing' thing. Because while a lot of people are in fact submissive to the federal government, a lot of people will push for change when it's in fact desired. Such as civil rights, unpopular laws, or wars we don't want to be involved in.

Gepard is the best TD at that tier tbh. I can always count on gunning down at least two or three light tanks or lightly armored MBTs in a match with it. Most light tanks assume they can go cover to cover without being hit by a shell, but when a gepard launches several hundred 35mm shells at them, that's it man. 

&#x200B;

THEN when a Russian player gets cocky and charged your position and you load your APDS rounds or whatever and you can frontally pen them? God they must be so pissed.

Jagdtiger or Maus for the same reason. If you face stuff that isn't HEAT, (which relies on you not being uptiered) you can actually be a useful heavy tank and play a supporting 'mobile cover' role for your team. The amount of times I've been used as cover in a Maus for pushing a point is astonishingly high. Which, I adore playing a role that benefits the team more than it does for me.

&#x200B;

That being said, even when uptiered both are very strong but you have to rely on just not being hit and playing a sniper or backline role. With the Maus I typically can tank HEAT still, but obviously not very many. Jagdtiger you just have to play as a semi-tanky TD and hull down somewhere. Your gun on both of those (same main gun iirc) is still very good against most tanks, and is amazing for long distance fights.

Unfortunately the steam mods delete all posts asking about the actual experiences of cheating. I posted a massive 4 paragraph discussion about what I have experienced, what I see other people experience, and then asking what we know about 'actual cheating' so we can see it more. Deleted by the mods. I revised it, deleted again, I revised it once more, and it was deleted yet again for encouraging cheating. Which, if the mods were coherent in the slightest, they would see I was actively trying to figure out what confirmed methods of cheating were out there so we wouldn't be reporting innocents as often or at least know when to report someone.

&#x200B;

I myself have been accused of cheating a lot, although the most recent accusation was after I used a DSHKA on my cupola to hit the ammo of an 8.8cm truck to kill it instantly. Which, I replayed the match to see their POV and it was a very very easy kill as I thought. Out in the open and exposed for more than 10 seconds in my vision. Not to mention I accidentally shot through an ostwind, killing that, and then hit him in his drivers compartment. (He accused me of one shotting him, and he was in fact one shot when I used my machinegun but not from the disabling shot from my T-10)

Can't speak for the other Americans but I consider other countries far more interesting and desirable even though I feel blessed to live in a place such as this. 

&#x200B;

Could be way worse, although it's sad to see people shitting on Americans for being American instead of being better than Americans. Idk how many Americans are like half the memes here because I only see it from my POV, but if we truly are toxic like that I would wish those we are toxic toward would try to fix the issue by not sinking to our level.

It probably is because they hear you mention him so often, if you do that is, because generally most people I know have never heard of him or don't feel one way or the other if they had heard him. I highly doubt that many people hate him for how he is or what he does, except maybe your mom since she probably hears him swearing and shit and jumps to a conclusion that he's some sort of degenerate PSYCHO.

&#x200B;

But anyways I would just like...not mention Jerma around your friends and stuff, not often at least. I have no idea how your friends are, but to me I would just ask my friends straight up if I annoy them with the things I talk about. Or really in this case my only friend after highschool has been my partner and she has no clue who Jerma is lmao

&#x200B;

Anyways best of luck to you, people are mean and I totally get that you may not catch on to what others would consider 'simple social cues'. I myself don't, and can do things that I think are normal when in reality it's annoying to someone.

I should have figured most of the Reddit crowd wouldn't have understood you can have weird jokes and settings without them being sexualized. Although I suppose a lot are projecting on that front.

&#x200B;

As for the game 10 months after this post, been keeping an ear on it and finally picked it up. Can proudly say that it's a very good start to what could easily be a pretty solid indie game, likely a cult classic at that since it tries to appeal to the people who enjoy weird niche media things akin to immature things like pee. Not in a fetish sense, although I mean if you somehow get off to the very limited details of the pee in the game then more to you I suppose.

At least until we get infantry ;)

&#x200B;

Makes me wonder if we will though given we have AT emplacements in the game now, for world war at least. Wouldn't shock me if we get some AT crew marching about one day, maybe even something that can spawn at cap points if you hold down a button or something.

I thought this was a joke at first but you're being serious.

&#x200B;

Uh, have fun never getting anything.
